    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Green. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe request may include `birthDate` (ISO); when present, the response returns `ageBand` computed against `registrationDate`. Since acceptance tests create via `POST /api/owners` then read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, `birthDate` is persisted and `ageBand` derived on every read.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, regenerating both DTOs on build.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field with `@Column(name = \"birth_date\")` plus getter/setter. MapStruct's `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` auto-maps it by name, so no pipeline function needed.\n\n3. **`util/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 `of(birthDate, registrationDate)` returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+) via `Period.between(...).getYears()`, or `null` when no birth date.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand` mapping expression calling `AgeBand.of(owner.getBirthDate(), owner.getRegistrationDate())`, matching the existing derived-field style. Computing it in the mapper means both the create response and the GET response stay consistent.\n\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (hsqldb/h2 are what the tests use).\n\nI followed the existing derived-field conventions (plain-string band like `locality`/`contactPreference`, computed in the mapper against the already business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`) rather than adding a new OfficeFloor pipeline step, since the value is a pure read-time derivation of stored state.",
